# Normalise line endings.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is set on this machine, so the index already stores LF —
# but the worktree ended up mixed (30 files LF, 23 CRLF) because different
# tools write differently on Windows. That mix makes git report changes to
# files nobody edited.
#
# It matters more here than usual: PLAN.md §8.2 rule 4 and CLAUDE.md invariant
# 10 require a full rebuild to reproduce byte-identical output, and the golden
# fixtures are the regression baseline for that. A fixture whose bytes shift
# with the checkout is not a baseline.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the worktree too, so the working copy matches the index on
# every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit, so a future .gitattributes edit cannot accidentally exempt them.
*.py   text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

# Archived source files are bytes, not text. PLAN.md §4.4 archives every
# fetched file permanently and content-hashed; any EOL translation would
# change the hash and break the reparse path. (These live under /data/ and are
# gitignored — this is belt and braces for anything that escapes it.)
*.pdf  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.xls  binary
*.duckdb binary
*.db   binary
